WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.820
- As always, we are gonna end
with something super uplifting

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.750
from social media.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.778
This is #What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:07.770
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.660
All right, I've seen little girls obsessed

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.060
with dressing as princesses, superheros,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.180
even Ruth Bader Ginsburg, a
superhero in her own rite.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.310
But one five-year-old has a fascination

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.930
I've never heard from a kid,

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.700
and it's perfect to feature as part

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.930
of Women's History Month.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.366
Here is her momma explaining.

00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:24.199
(air whooshing)

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:26.310
- My five-year-old was Eleanor Roosevelt

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.540
for the Presidents' Day thing at school.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.600
And ever since she put on that costume,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.880
she has not taken it off.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.910
She wants an Eleanor
Roosevelt birthday party.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.330
She's asked for a
stuffed Eleanor Roosevelt

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.800
to sleep with at night.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.150
She has asked that I refer
to her as your ladyship

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.418
from now on.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:51.368
(audience laughing)

00:00:51.368 --> 00:00:52.370
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.370
- Oh my god.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.830
A couple months later,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.810
Essie's interest in Eleanor Roosevelt

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.460
is as strong as ever, y'all.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.720
We have her and her momma,
Liz, on the line. (laughing)

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.626
(audience cheering)

00:01:03.626 --> 00:01:04.459
What's up, Essie?

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:06.360
What's up, Liz?

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.730
Oh my gosh, I love you, Essie.
- Hey, Kelly.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.500
- Oh, Essie, you look great.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.240
So Liz, this all started, like you said,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.620
with a Presidents' Day project.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.400
So how quickly did you
realize Essie was Eleanor fan

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.600
for life, like she was deep?

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.790
(audience laughing)

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.660
- Yeah, so, I put her and
her sister to bed one night

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.610
and went down to the kitchen

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.740
and poured myself a glass of wine.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.370
And then I turned around
and there she was standing

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.110
in the dark

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.438
with her Eleanor Roosevelt costume on

00:01:36.438 --> 00:01:37.271
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:39.270
over her pajamas.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.508
And honestly, it was a
jump scare at that point.

00:01:42.508 --> 00:01:43.341
(audience laughing)

00:01:43.341 --> 00:01:46.267
But then, after that, she said,

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.180
"Mommy can we go to Target

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.670
and get an Eleanor Roosevelt doll

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.320
because I wanna sleep with her tonight?"

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.280
And I said, "Well, they don't
make those kinds of dolls

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.240
at Target."
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.110
But the internet came through
because I posted on TikTok

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.733
that I was looking for
Eleanor Roosevelt merch

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:05.566
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:08.070
and people from all around the country

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.103
have sent us the most amazing things.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:16.380
We got a handwritten letter
from Eleanor Roosevelt,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.730
and we got a "Life" magazine
with her portrait on the cover.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.430
And it's just been so amazing.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.380
- Aw, that is so awesome.
(audience applauding)

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.850
Gosh, she's so cute.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.910
So, Essie, do you love your Eleanor doll?

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.710
- Yeah, yes, yes,

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.840
and yes.
(audience laughing)

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.640
- I love it. (laughing)
- Yes.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.370
- Yes, that's an affirmative
answer, I like it.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.080
So, Liz, what does it mean to you

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.540
that Essie's just so
into Eleanor Roosevelt?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.530
I think that's so cool.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.950
Like what a cool like
superhero figure for a kid.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.273
- I know, I love it.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.450
I've done a lot of
reflection on it actually,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.190
and it's just like,

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.620
it's so important for children to learn

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.770
about all these amazing
historical figures.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.250
And it's really inspired
me to research on my own

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.100
and find out more about women's history

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.320
and Eleanor Roosevelt.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.810
And I've learned that she was

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.870
one of the First Ladies
that had news conferences,

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.270
and she really revolutionized

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.430
the entire job of First Lady.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.300
She changed it from hostess
and president's wife

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.690
to a woman who would
step in for her husband

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:25.530
when he was sick.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.640
And,
- Yeah.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.800
- I'm just, I hope that Essie knows that

00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:31.830
- It's possible.
- These are the kinda barriers

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:35.212
that she can break and that
she can change the world.

00:03:35.212 --> 00:03:36.720
(audience applauding)
- Yeah.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.810
Oh my gosh, Essie, you are so cute.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.150
Aw, I love it.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.310
Well, thank you so much, Liz, for sharing,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.710
and Essie, I'm so, you look so adorable

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.030
and I love your doll.

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.560
Thank you y'all for being on the show.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.790
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.964
- Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:03:53.964 --> 00:03:54.797
- [Speaker] It's so cute.

00:03:54.797 --> 00:03:56.010
- All right, that's not all, though.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.750
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.490
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:00.540
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.360
want to celebrate
fearless, inspiring kiddos

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:04.200
just like Essie.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.760
So they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.759
How's that sound?

00:04:06.759 --> 00:04:08.390
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.298
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:10.298 --> 00:04:12.750
That's amazing.
- $1,000?

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.172
- Oh, thank you.
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:15.172 --> 00:04:16.542
- Thank you, ladies.
(crowd applauding continues)

00:04:16.542 --> 00:04:17.375
Have a blessed day.

00:04:17.375 --> 00:04:19.478
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:04:19.478 --> 00:04:21.813
Chrissy Teigen, Matt Iseman, Lucas Gage,

00:04:21.813 --> 00:04:24.210
Jenny, Jemmy, and Easton Corbin.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.620
Have a great day, y'all, and if it's not,

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.120
try and change it.

